  "mach:judgement": "Assess",
  "mach:judgementReason": "A current (2026) openly licensed medical speech-to-text model with ungated CC-BY-4.0 weights and practical on-device deployment options (NeMo, MLX, GGUF), targeting a real and high-value clinical workflow — ambient/dictation transcription for GP consultations, medication review, and procedure language. Built on the well-regarded NVIDIA Parakeet TDT backbone. Marked Assess rather than Adopt for several reasons. (1) It is a v1/beta release from a single vendor (Omi Health) with no independent benchmarking or adoption track record yet. (2) The reported evaluation is small (7.18 hours) and partly synthetic, and full training-data provenance is not disclosed, so generalisation to real clinical accents/noise is unverified. (3) Clinical transcription sits in EU AI Act high-risk-candidate territory; the authors themselves require human review and disclaim clinical-decision use. Useful now for teams prototyping local medical-scribe pipelines who can validate accuracy on their own data; revisit for Adopt once independent evaluation and broader adoption exist. The companion clinical-note safety benchmark is cataloged separately as medical-note-eval (datasets).",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-06-24",
